{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.md","line":87,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","line":183,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[a geodesic attains equality in the Schwarz comparison]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed, def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.3}\n  For a geodesic $\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$ with integrable speed and squared speed,\n  $$\n  L(\\gamma)^2 = (b-a)\\,E(\\gamma).\n  $$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed}\n  \\sketch\n  A geodesic has constant speed (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed}), so its parameter is\n  proportional to arc length, which is precisely the equality case of\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz}.\n\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[a geodesic attains equality in the Schwarz comparison] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368392d322d332d67656f64657369632d657175616c697479\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-1-constspeed\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23def%3Adc-ch9-2-2-energy\">↗ def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch9:2.3</span></span>For a geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$</span> with integrable speed and squared speed, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  L(\\gamma )^2 = (b-a)\\, E(\\gamma ).  \\]\">\\[  L(\\gamma )^2 = (b-a)\\, E(\\gamma ).  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-1-constspeed\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed</a> \\sketch A geodesic has constant speed (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-1-constspeed\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368332d322d312d636f6e73747370656564\">section lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed</a>), so its parameter is proportional to arc length, which is precisely the equality case of <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368392d322d322d7363687761727a\">section 1</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-arclength-bridge","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","label":"def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-equality-case"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[a geodesic attains equality in the Schwarz comparison]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed, def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.3}\n  For a geodesic $\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$ with integrable speed and squared speed,\n  $$\n  L(\\gamma)^2 = (b-a)\\,E(\\gamma).\n  $$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed}\n  \\sketch\n  A geodesic has constant speed (\\cref{lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed}), so its parameter is\n  proportional to arc length, which is precisely the equality case of\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz}.\n\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-1-constspeed","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}